         "smile": "inlove",
         "source_menu": [
            {
               "type": 1,
               "uuid": "d603e3a0-cf2a-497d-9fc3-cfed73743515",
               "text": "Texto Original",
               "page": "https://www.historytracers.org/index.html?page=class_content&arg=d603e3a0-cf2a-497d-9fc3-cfed73743515",
               "date_time": {
                  "type": "gregory",
                  "year": "2026",
                  "month": "",
                  "day": ""
               }
            }
         ],
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "#### Símbolos Diferentes, el Mismo Número\n\nAl llegar al 5, ambos pueblos tenían un símbolo propio. Los etrusco-romanos usaban la mitad de su símbolo del 10 (X); los mesoamericanos usaban una barra que, suponemos, representa los dedos juntos.",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<p data-custom=\"missing-numbers-five\"></p>",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ],
         "desc": null,
         "next": "2ea7e2aa-4103-4334-8323-0026216f106b",
         "prev": "",
         "jumpTo": "",
         "answer": null,
